// codebase_audit_live.jsonl — issue #413: "read a codebase, audit it for a specific issue, and
// report back" — a distinct capability from generic coding (write/run a script) and from
// research (web search). Exercises read/search-heavy tool paths (grep/read/codegraph-style
// exploration, delegate_to_code_agent) and grounds the judge check on whether the report cites
// REAL file paths/findings from this repo rather than generic/hallucinated advice. Two GitHub-
// MCP variants point at the public repo (read-only, safe). LIVE lane only.
{"id": "audit_tool_contract_gap_live", "prompt": "look through this codebase's tool registry and skill files and check whether every MCP server listed under mcp_servers in config/config.yaml actually has a matching SKILL.md — report back which ones (if any) are missing", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_code_agent", "read_file", "search_files", "grep"], "response_excludes": ["i cannot", "i don't have access"], "max_duration_s": 180}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "verifiable ground truth exists (docs/guides/SERVICES_AND_MCPS.md requires this 1:1 mapping) -- a good report should name real files, not generic advice"}
{"id": "audit_security_pattern_live", "prompt": "search this codebase for any place that builds a shell command by string concatenation instead of a safe argument list (a potential command-injection risk) and report what you find with file:line references", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_code_agent", "search_files", "grep"], "max_duration_s": 180}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "read-only static audit; response_grounded should catch a report that cites plausible-sounding but nonexistent files/lines"}
{"id": "audit_specific_bug_repro_live", "prompt": "look at src/infrastructure/tools/registry.py in this repo and tell me whether generate_presentation, render_marp, and render_animation are actually registered there, or if any are missing", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_code_agent", "read_file", "grep"], "response_includes": ["generate_presentation"], "max_duration_s": 150}, "judge": ["response_grounded"], "note": "narrow, checkable claim (mirrors the real 2026-07-05 incident referenced in visual_artifacts_live.jsonl) -- verifies the audit actually reads the file instead of guessing"}
{"id": "audit_github_repo_readonly_live", "prompt": "on GitHub, look at MatthewLoyed/AIAssistant's src/core/orchestration/nodes/routing.py and tell me what decides whether a turn goes to the plan lane vs the agent lane", "category": "agent", "expect": {"response_excludes": ["i cannot", "i don't have access"], "max_duration_s": 150}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "same audit task but sourced via the github MCP (get_file_contents) instead of local file tools -- read-only, safe"}
{"id": "audit_dependency_freshness_live", "prompt": "check this project's Python dependency pins (requirements or pyproject) for FastAPI and LangGraph and tell me the pinned versions", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_code_agent", "read_file", "grep"], "max_duration_s": 120}, "judge": ["response_grounded"], "note": "simple, verifiable extraction task -- catches an agent that answers from training-data guesses about typical versions instead of actually reading the pin file"}
